{
  "case_id": "2018-18-525",
  "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Colleen E. Roh Sinzdak (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SINZDAK: Well, Justice Ginsburg, I think the important question with respect to jurisdiction is whether the agency has been empowered to attempt to resolve a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Colleen E. Roh Sinzdak (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SINZDAK: It -- it waives the immunity, but, again, the question is how broad a waiver is there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But you place some considerable reliance on 2000e-5(f)(3), the jurisdictional provision for Title VII, but what if that didn't exist, so that a plaintiff would have to rely solely on 1331? Would you have the same argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You would agree to that? The EEOC has no authority to decide an issue that the parties dispute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. SinzdaK",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SINZDAK: There's de novo review of what the EEOC does decide, which is cause or no cause. I would also say it's performing a very effective funneling function regardless."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress created a scheme that limited the jurisdiction of the -- of the judiciary by giving authority first to an agency that would resolve some of the claims so that the judiciary never has to pass on it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. SinzdaK",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. SINZDAK: I think because the incentives of the -- that a defendant has aren't precisely aligned with the system-related goals that the exhaustion requirement is vindicating."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So, when it is individualized, to pick up on Justice Sotomayor's question from earlier, are you saying that we should usually presume that Congress intended an administrative exhaustion scheme to be jurisdictional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: What sort of empirical evidence are you -- are you looking for?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. MELKONIAN",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. MELKONIAN: It would be very hard to -- to find it, Your Honor. I -- I concede that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: How many cases have you find like this one where there's been a finding by a circuit court that a party has basically waived the mandatory rule?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: What do you say to the Chief Justice's concern that this is a statute that predates Arbaugh?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-18-525",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "22ba1b65f97cdc74b6acf83af10f3ddeb459879a4b3b5124a5d3303f20ea1670",
      "evidence_id": "ev-22ba1b65f97c-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
